    "message": {
      "content": "# Validation Checklist for Multi-Node Language-Model Serving Systems\n\n## Purpose and Scope\n\nThis checklist validates that a distributed LLM serving system (tensor-parallel, pipeline-parallel, expert-parallel, or data-parallel deployments) behaves correctly under realistic conditions. It is designed to catch silent failures \u2014 wrong outputs, dropped requests, misattributed latency \u2014 that single-node testing misses.\n\n---\n\n## 1. Configuration Identity\n\n**Goal:** Prove every node is running the exact same logical system.\n\n- [ ] **Model artifact hash.** Record SHA-256 of model weights, tokenizer files, and config files on *every* node. Verify all hashes match. Do not trust \"same path\" \u2014 verify content.\n- [ ] **Build/binary identity.** Record version, commit SHA, and build hash of the serving binary/framework on each node. Confirm identical.\n- [ ] **Dependency fingerprint.** Capture `pip freeze` / conda env / container image digest per node. Flag any drift, including \"harmless\" transitive dependencies.\n- [ ] **Runtime configuration diff.** Dump the effective runtime config (not the config file \u2014 the *resolved* config, including env vars, CLI overrides, and defaults) on each node and diff them. Explicitly whitelist expected per-node differences (e.g., `node_rank`, local device IDs).\n- [ ] **Parallelism topology.** Record tensor-parallel size, pipeline-parallel size, expert-parallel size, and world size. Verify `world_size == TP \u00d7 PP \u00d7 EP \u00d7 DP` (per your framework's formula) and that it matches the actual number of participating processes.\n- [ ] **Precision settings.** Confirm dtype (fp16/bf16/int8/fp8), quantization config, KV-cache dtype, and any attention-kernel selection are identical across nodes. A single node falling back to fp32 or a different kernel is a correctness and performance hazard.\n- [ ]",
      "reasoning": "",
      "role": "assistant"
    },
